A||||3||Fleabitdog||Need help## starter and ig mod||||1||
Z||000000||Fleabitdog||09-27-2000||10:33 AM||||I have an 88GT. Since I bought it, when you go to start it you usually get a click. Next try it starts. Once in a while after it has run for a while when I try to start it I get nothing. Wait a while and it starts. It has been doing this more frequent. I am going to replace the ig mod and if that does not do it the starter. The mod is special order from the dealer and I need it right away. is there any danger in trying a used mod? If not will all year ig mods and starters fit my 88? Thanks for your help     Dave ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||09-27-2000||03:11 PM||||You problem is the starter, battery or cables, if all it does is click. If t ends up being the starter then replace it and find/buy/make a heat sheild for it if it doesn't have one.<P>Try taking it to autozone or someplace and let them hook up the charging/starting system analyzer to it. It's usually free. That may help you find what's going on.<P>Now if it was turning over and not getting spark then it would be ignition.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fleabitdog||09-28-2000||11:27 PM||||Thanks Ogre. I replaced the starter yesterday. It is still doing the same thing. Tomorrow I will make a heat shield and clean all my cables. Should take care of the prob. At least now I have a spare starter.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||09-29-2000||12:32 AM||||Don't forget the easy thing and have the battery checked. Sounds like a heat problem. The battery may be getting overly sensitive to heat affecting the crank amps. If its getting up in years that may be your simple problem. <P>I agree that the ign mod would not make your engine click, it would turn and turn and not start then if it was the mod or pick up coil.||||reg||1
